Q1. What is the Command Design Pattern?
Why do we need it?

Interview Ready Answer

The Command Pattern is a
Behavioral Design Pattern
that encapsulates a request
or action as an object.

Instead of executing an action
directly,

the request is wrapped inside
a Command object,

which can later be executed,
queued, logged or undone.

------------------------------------------------------------

Why do we need Command Pattern?

• Reduce Tight Coupling.
• Encapsulate Requests.
• Support Undo/Redo.
• Support Command Queue.
• Support Logging.
• Support Remote Execution.
• Improve Maintainability.

------------------------------------------------------------

What problem does it solve?

Without Command Pattern

Remote

↓

if(TV)

↓

turnOnTV()

else if(Fan)

↓

turnOnFan()

else if(AC)

↓

turnOnAC()

Problems

• Tight Coupling.
• Difficult to Extend.
• Difficult to Maintain.

------------------------------------------------------------

With Command Pattern

Remote

↓

Command Interface

↓

TVOnCommand

FanOnCommand

ACOnCommand

↓

Receiver

The Remote only executes

command.execute();

without knowing
the actual implementation.

