Q2. Roles of Client, Invoker,
Command, Concrete Command
and Receiver

Interview Ready Answer

1. Client

Creates the Command object
and assigns it to the Invoker.

Example

Person using the Remote.

------------------------------------------------------------

2. Invoker

Triggers the Command.

Example

Remote Control.

It simply calls

command.execute();

------------------------------------------------------------

3. Command

An interface that declares

execute();

------------------------------------------------------------

4. Concrete Command

Implements the Command interface.

• Stores a reference
  to the Receiver.

• Calls the appropriate
  method on the Receiver.

Example

TVOnCommand

------------------------------------------------------------

5. Receiver

Performs the actual work.

Example

TV

↓

turnOn()

------------------------------------------------------------

Working Flow

Client

↓

Invoker (Remote)

↓

Command Interface

↓

Concrete Command

↓

Receiver

↓

Actual Work

