Q3. Difference between Command Pattern
and Strategy Pattern

Interview Ready Answer

Command Pattern

• Behavioral Design Pattern.
• Encapsulates a request
  as an object.
• Focuses on executing actions.
• Supports Undo/Redo,
  Logging,
  Queue,
  Remote Execution.

Example

Remote

↓

TVOnCommand

↓

TV

------------------------------------------------------------

Strategy Pattern

• Behavioral Design Pattern.
• Encapsulates multiple
  interchangeable algorithms.
• Focuses on selecting
  one algorithm at runtime.
• Removes if-else/switch.
• Reduces Tight Coupling.

Example

Payment

↓

UPIStrategy

CardStrategy

NetBankingStrategy

↓

Client Chooses One

------------------------------------------------------------

